        <title>Keel</title>
        <item>
            <title>1.15.0</title>
            <pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 15:50:43 +0530</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>254</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>1.15.0</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <description><![CDATA[<ul>
  <li>Updates: an &quot;Include in Update All&quot; button beside &quot;Open Homebrew&quot; lets Update All update your Homebrew packages too (&quot;Leave out&quot; turns it off again). It&#x27;s the same setting as in Settings.</li>
  <li>Apps whose new version macOS won&#x27;t open, because Homebrew disabled the cask for failing Apple&#x27;s check, now say so on their row and offer the Download Page instead of an Update button that would fail. They aren&#x27;t counted as waiting.</li>
  <li>When Keel refuses a download for its signature, it remembers that version and doesn&#x27;t try it again; the row offers the Download Page until a newer version comes out.</li>
  <li>GitHub releases with several Mac files: Keel now skips command-line tools, picks the build for the newest macOS your Mac runs, and prefers the file named after the app, instead of giving up.</li>
  <li>Cancelling the App Store&#x27;s prompt during an update now shows &quot;Cancelled · still available&quot; instead of a failure, with no popup.</li>
  <li>App Store errors now show one clean line instead of the App Store tool&#x27;s progress bars.</li>
  <li>The popup after Update All lists at most five apps, so its OK button is always on screen.</li>
  <li>An update that failed but is still available is counted at the top of Updates, instead of &quot;Everything is up to date&quot;.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
